{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"I found two causes: publication stores the UTC calendar date instead of the author’s local date, and rendering converts an invented noon timestamp instead of the post’s actual creation time. The feed also sorts by date, which can misorder posts around timezone boundaries. I’ll use the stored timestamp for display and ordering, and the author’s zone for the stored date."}}
